Plan Conference Services Our Campus Diversity and Inclusion Human Resources & Employment Our rich liberal arts tradition, sound career focus, and empowering and supportive environment prepare our students for success. Academic Excellence About Us Close X Search Academics Academics Undergraduate Degrees and Programs Continuing Education Bachelor's and Associate's Degrees Graduate Degrees and Programs School of Business and Technology School of Nursing and Health Sciences Neurodiversity Center for Excellence Program for Advancement of Learning (PAL) Social Achievement in Learning (SAIL) Academic Student Resources Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Undergraduate Admission Tuition and Financial Aid Continuing and Graduate Admission Affordability for Future Students Request Information - Undergraduate Apply Visit Been Accepted? Contact Admission Office Student Life Student Life Living at Curry Clubs and Activities Student Center Dining Student Services Health and Wellness Public Safety Accessibility Services Curry Bookstore Athletics Athletics Colonels NCAA Athletics Athletics Video: #BleedPurple Recruit Me Club Sports Intramurals Fitness Center The Curry Fund for Athletics Shop Colonels Athletics Contact Athletics Alumni Alumni Events and Reunions Update My Information Benefits and Resources Support Curry 1879 Planned Giving Society Volunteer Alumni Career Resources Employer Matching Gifts Contact Alumni Relations About Us About Us Why Curry? Fast Facts Mission and Leadership News and Events Strategic Plan Conference Services Our Campus Diversity and Inclusion Human Resources & Employment Visit Apply Give Contact Curry College | Home Academics Academic Student Resources Career & Experiential Learning (CXL) Career & Experiential Learning (CXL) Groundbreaking Experiences and Exceptional Resources You’re going to go places. Career & Experiential Learning (CXL) will get you started on your journey. We’ll help you identify your career goals, connect you with internship experiences, and sharpen your job-ready skills. Our services don’t end when you graduate, either: As a Curry alum, you can rely on our services for as long as you need. Contact Career & Experiential Learning 617-333-2195 careerdevelopment@curry.edu 65A Atherton Street Office Hours: 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m., Monday–Friday Make an Appointment The Curry Commitment Has Launched! Our Job Promise, Made for You Curry College is the only college in Massachusetts to offer a job guarantee program! This four-year program prepares undergraduate students to enter the workforce seamlessly after graduation by integrating career readiness programming and experiential learning opportunities into the undergraduate experience.  Through this program, students receive support and services that prepare them to take the next steps towards their career shortly after graduation. Learn More about the Curry Commitment Video: Our Job Promise, Made for You Careers and Internships Career planning at Curry starts during your first year here. From the basics of building a resume to using Handshake to find a meaningful internship, we’ll help you build a foundation that lasts. Find out more by connecting with us at careerdevelopment@curry.edu . Handshake Make an Appointment Internships Experiential Learning at Curry Student Career Services Current students are encouraged to utilize Career & Experiential Learning early and often. We offer a wide variety of academic and professional programs and resources to give our students an edge in a challenging and competitive job market. Student Career Services Alumni Career Services Curry College Alumni are welcome to utilize the resources provided by Career & Experiential Learning to help tackle your own career challenges. We also encourage successful Curry alums to partner with us to aid current students in their career exploration. Alumni Career Services Employer Partner Resources We invite businesses of all kinds to partner with us here at Curry College Career & Experiential Learning. As a Curry Connector, you will gain access to a pool of bright, motivated, and eager students who are ready to make a contribution to your company. Employer Partners Become a Curry Connector Career-Focused Events Career & Experiential Learning (CXL) and campus partners offer opportunities throughout the year to help you explore careers, build professional skills, and connect with employers, alumni, and industry professionals. Career Events & Programs Meet Our CXL Staff: Derek Cameron Associate Director for Employer Relations Department Career & Experiential Learning Phone (617) 333-2195 Email derek.cameron@curry.edu Read full bio Alyssa Devlin Assistant Director, Career & Internship Advising Department Career & Experiential Learning Phone (617) 333-2260 Email alyssa.devlin@curry.edu Read full bio Julia Himmelberger Career Advisor Department Career & Experiential Learning Phone Email julia.himmelberger@curry.edu Read full bio Maeve McCann Administrative Assistant Department Career & Experiential Learning Phone (617) 333-2195 Email maeve.mccann@curry.edu Read full bio Tamara Menghi Executive Director Department Career & Experiential Learning Phone (617) 333-2195 Email tamara.menghi@curry.edu Read full bio Claire Pocius Career Advisor Department Career & Experiential Learning Phone Email claire.pocius@curry.edu Read full bio See All Faculty and Staff Meet Our Faculty Internship Facilitators: Dr. Shawn Scott Accounting, Business Administration, Computer Science, Entrepreneurship, Finance, Management, Marketing, Sport and Recreation Management Contact Professor Scott Dr. Elizabeth Wade Biochemistry, Biology, Environmental Science, Forensic Science Contact Professor Wade Professor Jerry Gibbs Communication: TV/Film, Social Media, Journalism, Public Relations, Sports Communication, Video Games Contact Professor Gibbs Dr. Rebecca Kendall Community Advocacy and Justice, Criminology and Criminal Justice, Sociology, Social Work Contact Professor Kendall Dr. Lindsay Illich Creative Writing Contact Professor Illich Dr. Courtney James Exercise Science Contact Professor James Dr. Ryan Theroux General Education Contact Professor Theroux Professor Alison Poor-Donahue Graphic Design Contact Professor Poor-Donahue Dr. Jen Balboni Pre-Law Contact Professor Balboni Dr. Mia Khera Psychology, Brain and Cognitive Sciences, Art Therapy Contact Professor Khera Professor Katherine Begin Education Contact Professor Begin Dr. Colby Zongol Public Health Contact Professor Zongol Pre-Law Advising: Dr. Jen Balboni Dr. Jen Balboni advises Curry students who are interested in pursuing law school. Dr. Balboni is a Professor in the Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice. She completed her Ph.D. in Law, Policy and Society at Northeastern University, with a focus on criminal justice and restorative justice. She also has a Master’s Degree in Criminal Justice from Northeastern University. Meet/Contact Professor Balboni Begin Your Curry Adventure Chart your path to the future via Curry’s Career & Experiential Learning services. Participate in the Curry Commitment Program, develop career readiness skills, get on-the-job training in an internship, prepare to apply to graduate school, and more! Make an Appointment Request Information Apply Now Contact Admission Curry College 1071 Blue Hill Ave, Milton, MA 02186 617-333-0500 Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Academic Calendar Curry News Curry Events Support Curry Sitemap myCurry Portal Human Resources & Employment Course Catalog Notices and Disclosures Privacy Policy Title IX ©2026 Curry College NOTICE OF NON-DISCRIMINATION: Curry College is committed to providing equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students, and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, age, ethnic or national origin or ancestry, veteran status, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, veteran or military status, membership in Uniformed Services, or any category protected by applicable state and federal laws. Curry College does not discriminate on the basis of any protected class in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan program, and athletic and other school-administered programs. Similarly, Curry College is committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. See Commitment to Non-Discrimination . TikTok Instagram Youtube Twitter Facebook Linked in Curry College Website Disclosure We use cookies to make interactions with our websites and services easy and meaningful. By continuing to use this website, you consent to Curry College’s usage of cookies and similar technologies in accordance with the college’s Cookie Notice . ×"
