e Services Our Campus Diversity and Inclusion Human Resources & Employment Our rich liberal arts tradition, sound career focus, and empowering and supportive environment prepare our students for success. Academic Excellence About Us Close X Search Academics Academics Undergraduate Degrees and Programs Continuing Education Bachelor's and Associate's Degrees Graduate Degrees and Programs School of Business and Technology School of Nursing and Health Sciences Neurodiversity Center for Excellence Program for Advancement of Learning (PAL) Social Achievement in Learning (SAIL) Academic Student Resources Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Undergraduate Admission Tuition and Financial Aid Continuing and Graduate Admission Affordability for Future Students Request Information - Undergraduate Apply Visit Been Accepted? Contact Admission Office Student Life Student Life Living at Curry Clubs and Activities Student Center Dining Student Services Health and Wellness Public Safety Accessibility Services Curry Bookstore Athletics Athletics Colonels NCAA Athletics Athletics Video: #BleedPurple Recruit Me Club Sports Intramurals Fitness Center The Curry Fund for Athletics Shop Colonels Athletics Contact Athletics Alumni Alumni Events and Reunions Update My Information Benefits and Resources Support Curry 1879 Planned Giving Society Volunteer Alumni Career Resources Employer Matching Gifts Contact Alumni Relations About Us About Us Why Curry? Fast Facts Mission and Leadership News and Events Strategic Plan Conference Services Our Campus Diversity and Inclusion Human Resources & Employment Visit Apply Give Contact Curry College | Home Academics Academic Student Resources Career & Experiential Learning (CXL) Alumni Career Services Alumni Career Services Career & Experiential Learning (CXL) Explore Section The Curry Commitment Career Outcomes and Success Student Career Services Alumni Career Services Employer Partners Curry Connectors Internships for Academic Credit Experiential Learning Career Events & Programs Contact Career & Experiential Learning Contact Career & Experiential Learning 617-333-2195 careerdevelopment@curry.edu 65A Atherton Street Complimentary Career Tools for Life As an alum of Curry College, you are always welcome to use the resources provided by Career & Experiential Learning. We recognize that you have different challenges than current students whether it's undertaking a career change, dealing with a job loss, or brushing up on your job search skills.  We also encourage successful Curry alumni to partner with us to aid current students in their career exploration. Services Available to Curry College Alumni: Access to Handshake Within 6 months of graduating from Curry Please update your Handshake account with your new email address. You can “add another email” by logging in to Handshake -->clicking on your initials or photo in the top right-hand corner-->Settings-->“Account Access.”  With your Handshake account, you can continue to participate in workshops, presentations, career fairs, job applications, and more. Beyond 6 months from Curry graduation Please email careerdevelopment@curry.edu for help updating your account. Please share your new personal email address and request that your Handshake email on record be changed. Once that change is made by CXL, you will be able to reset your password and access Handshake to view workshops, presentations, career fairs, job opportunities, and more. Career Advising Curry College alumni can schedule one-on-one career appointments with the Career & Experiential Learning team directly through Handshake. During peak times of the academic year, appointment availability for alumni may be limited as we prioritize current students; however, alumni continue to have full access to job and internship postings, events, workshops, and career fairs. Make an appointment through Handshake or call 617-333-2195 for help making an appointment. Networking Opportunities Staying connected with Curry College alumni strengthens your professional network and keeps you tied to a community that shares your educational experience. Alumni connections can lead to career insight, collaboration, referrals, and mentoring whether you’re exploring a career change, hiring talent, or simply exchanging ideas. You can access Curry alums in two ways. Handshake Log in to Handshake, then select “People” from the menu. Filter or scroll through the list of current students and alums to find fellow alums and message them directly to ask questions, seek advice, or request an informational chat. LinkedIn Use the search field to find Curry College and then visit the alumni page to reach out with a short, personalized message. What’s your status? Recent Grad? What’s your status? Whether you are already working, in graduate school, in the process of starting a business, engaged in volunteer service, or still defining your next professional steps, let us know how your career is shaping up after Curry and how we can assist you! Get in Touch! Take the next step We're excited you're considering our professional resources and services, available to our cherished Curry College Alumni. We look forward to helping you reach your career goals. You can also find more resources in the myCurry portal under the ' Career & Experiential Learning' tab. Schedule an Appointment Search Handshake (Jobs) CXL Resources at myCurry Contact Us Curry College 1071 Blue Hill Ave, Milton, MA 02186 617-333-0500 Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Academic Calendar Curry News Curry Events Support Curry Sitemap myCurry Portal Human Resources & Employment Course Catalog Notices and Disclosures Privacy Policy Title IX ©2026 Curry College NOTICE OF NON-DISCRIMINATION: Curry College is committed to providing equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students, and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, age, ethnic or national origin or ancestry, veteran status, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, veteran or military status, membership in Uniformed Services, or any category protected by applicable state and federal laws. Curry College does not discriminate on the basis of any protected class in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan program, and athletic and other school-administered programs. Similarly, Curry College is committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. See Commitment to Non-Discrimination . TikTok Instagram Youtube Twitter Facebook Linked in Curry College Website Disclosure We use cookies to make interactions with our websites and services easy and meaningful. By continuing to use this website, you consent to Curry College’s usage of cookies and similar technologies in accordance with the college’s Cookie Notice . ×"
