ducation, not a separate goal.  We are an inclusive community where embracing differences is essential to creating a safe and welcoming environment for exploration and learning, as well as personal and professional growth. Being a member of the Curry community means that your unique voice is a vital and valued part of all we do. Curry College is an equal opportunity employer that values and encourages diversity in its work force. If you are interested in applying for a position, please apply through one of the following links: Faculty and Staff Opportunities Student Employment : Visit Handshake via the myCurry Portal for a listing of available on-campus student positions. For more information about the student employment process, visit the myCurry Portal Student Employment (SEP) area . Please Note: In order to meet the degree criteria indicated in any individual position posted, candidate's degree(s) must be from an accredited College or University. Reference letters should not be emailed separately, but instead, please upload reference letters in the IE system when you are applying for a position of interest. This will keep all your application materials together in one electronic file. Curry College 1071 Blue Hill Ave, Milton, MA 02186 617-333-0500 Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Academic Calendar Curry News Curry Events Support Curry Sitemap myCurry Portal Human Resources & Employment Course Catalog Notices and Disclosures Privacy Policy Title IX ©2026 Curry College NOTICE OF NON-DISCRIMINATION: Curry College is committed to providing equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students, and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, age, ethnic or national origin or ancestry, veteran status, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, veteran or military status, membership in Unifor